<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0367">Remark <span data-tag="0367">5.3.2.14</span>.</a> Let $n$ be a nonnegative integer, and suppose we are given a diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  X(0) \rightarrow X(1) \rightarrow X(2) \rightarrow \cdots \rightarrow X(n). \]
</div>
<p> For each integer $0 \leq i \leq n$, let $\Delta ^ n_{\geq i}$ denote the nerve of the linearly ordered set $\{  i &lt; i+1 &lt; \cdots &lt; n \} $, which we regard as a simplicial subset of $\Delta ^ n$. Applying Remark <a data-tag="0252" href="/tag/0252">5.3.2.12</a> repeatedly, we can identify the mapping simplex $ \underset { \longrightarrow }{\mathrm{holim}}( X(0) \rightarrow \cdots \rightarrow X(n) )$ with the iterated pushout </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  (\Delta ^ n \times X(0)) {\coprod }_{ ( \Delta ^{n}_{\geq 1} \times X(0)) } (\Delta ^{n}_{\geq 1} \times X(1) ) {\coprod }_{ ( \Delta ^{n}_{\geq 2} \times X(1))} \cdots {\coprod }_{ (\{ n\}  \times X(n-1))} (\{ n\}  \times X(n)). \]
</div>
</article>
